      "displayName": "Real load (audit)",
      "layout": [
        {
          "widget": {
            "name": "audit_title",
            "multilineTextboxSpec": {
              "lines": [
                "## Your real Iceberg REST load (system.access.audit)\n\n",
                "Iceberg REST calls log as `uniformIcebergRestCatalog`; the UC calls underneath (getTable, generateTemporaryTableCredential) log as `unityCatalog`. **Peak QPS** is the busiest second in each minute: limits are enforced per second, so compare that, not the average, with the probe's onset. The audit log lagged about 10 minutes in our runs. 429s from the per-workspace edge limit did **not** show up here; 429s from the shared (cross-workspace) limit did. So a quiet audit log does not prove clients were never throttled.\n\n"
              ]
            }
          },
          "position": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 0,
            "width": 6,
            "height": 2
          }
        },
